  "verdict": "**NO \u2014 capping the A-run does not improve pipe 2.** B +0.5 pp [-8.9,+9.8], R +4.0 pp [-5.6,+13.5]; both intervals span zero, and across three training seeds the gains do not hold a sign. Temperature 0.7 does not rescue it. **The generation rule, in the one form the directive specified, is not the bottleneck for pipe 2.**\n\nBut the directive's 'no' branch \u2014 that the LIFT is then under suspicion \u2014 does not follow yet, and I am not claiming it. Two things sit in the way. **(1) R's pipe 3 moved 22.5% -> 31.5% under cap 24 while B's did not**, which is a resolution-dependent gain in the predicted direction, at the wrong obstacle. **(2) argmax is not a null result, it is an unmeasurable one**: it produces the most expert-like button statistics in the project and one trajectory to x=916, but it is n=1 per checkpoint and needs many start states rather than many seeds. **The lift's behavioural relevance is untested, not refuted.**",
